{
  "about": "Retrieval eval labels: query -> the résumé files a recruiter issuing it would want to see. Binary relevance. Corpus: the 31 synthetic résumés in resumes/ (summary.txt is not a résumé and is never relevant). DRAFTED BY THE MODEL; every query has status 'draft' until a human has checked it and set status to 'reviewed'. The eval runner marks results as not counting while any label is a draft.",
  "kinds": {
    "keyword": "the query names a specific, fairly rare term that appears in the relevant résumés",
    "semantic": "the query describes the need in words the relevant résumés mostly do not use",
    "filtered": "a query plus a min_years filter; relevant = matching résumés that pass the filter"
  },
